xt-wg for Debian
================

The source package builds three binaries:

  xt-wg-common   userspace iptables plugins (libxt_WG{OBFS,ANYCAST,PTCP}.so)
  xt-wg-source   kernel-module source for module-assistant
  xt-wg-dkms     kernel-module source for DKMS auto-rebuild

You almost always want xt-wg-common plus exactly one of xt-wg-dkms or
xt-wg-source.  They produce equivalent kernel modules via different
mechanisms.

  - xt-wg-dkms is set-and-forget: DKMS rebuilds xt_wg.ko automatically
    every time a new kernel is installed.  Requires linux-headers for
    each kernel.

  - xt-wg-source uses module-assistant.  Manual one-shot build per
    kernel: "m-a a-i xt-wg" produces an xt-wg-modules-$(uname -r)_*.deb.
    Useful when DKMS is unavailable or undesirable.

The kernel module ships as a single consolidated xt_wg.ko containing all
three xtables targets (WGOBFS, WGANYCAST, WGPTCP).  Module aliases mean
"modprobe xt_WGOBFS" / "modprobe xt_WGANYCAST" / "modprobe xt_WGPTCP"
still resolve to xt_wg.ko, so existing iptables auto-load behaviour and
/etc/modules-load.d entries keep working.

 -- Bingchen Gong <gongbingchen@gmail.com>
